# Fixtures & Environment Handling

## Test Data Rules

- All environments are defined in a single file: `tests/fixtures/environments.json`.
- The AML application runs at `https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506` by default (override via `BASE_URL` in `.env`).
- **2506 session login is enabled** — Playwright and MCP seed sign in through Clari5 Command Center (`/clari5-cc/login`) using `EMAIL` / `PASSWORD` (or `AML_USERNAME` / `AML_PASSWORD`) from `.env`. Default user: `QAUSER2`. Never commit the password. Skip auto-login with `PW_SKIP_AML_LOGIN=1`.
- **Do not generate or run unauthenticated / session-expiry / unauthorized-role cases** unless the user explicitly asks or sets `QA_INCLUDE_AUTH_CASES=1`. See `.cursor/rules/authentication-bypass-mandatory.mdc`.
- The `defaults` block provides shared values; per-env blocks override them.

Example structure:

tests/
  fixtures/
    environments.json   # All environments in one file
    env.ts              # Loader: merges defaults + env overrides
    test-fixture.ts     # Playwright custom fixture
    selector-map.json   # Shared selector mappings

Example `environments.json`:

{
  "defaults": {
    "validUsername": "",
    "validPassword": ""
  },
  "environments": {
    "dev": {
      "baseUrl": "https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506"
    },
    "uat": {
      "baseUrl": "https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506"
    },
    "production": {
      "baseUrl": "https://kadelamldev.customerxps.com:2506"
    }
  }
}

## Environment Selection

Environment is loaded from `.env` at runtime and merged into the test data:
- `ENV` → selects which environment block to use (default: dev)
- `BASE_URL` → overrides the environment's `baseUrl` if set
- `EMAIL` / `PASSWORD` (or `AML_USERNAME` / `AML_PASSWORD`) → 2506 Command Center session

## Parallel Multi-Environment Execution

The executor supports `--envs dev,uat` to run the same test cases
against multiple environments in parallel. Each env gets:
- Its own browser instance
- Its own results directory: `results/<env>/`
- Its own Allure results and screenshots

## Never:
- Hardcode URLs in spec files or page objects (use environments.json).
- Create separate JSON files per environment (use the unified config).
- Commit `.env` to source control.
